@startuml
title Sequence Diagram — Process Sale
autonumber
actor Pharmacist
participant "React POS" as POS
participant "ASP.NET Core\nSalesController" as API
participant MediatR as Mediator
participant "CreateSaleCommandHandler" as Handler
participant SaleService as Service
participant "EF Core Repositories /\nUnit of Work" as Persistence
database PostgreSQL as DB
participant AuditLogService as Audit

Pharmacist -> POS: Select items and quantities; enter payment/discount
POS -> API: POST /api/sales + Bearer JWT
API -> API: Authorize JWT; read user, role and branch claims
API -> Mediator: CreateSaleCommand(request, claims)
Mediator -> Handler: Handle(command)
Handler -> Service: CreateAsync(request, userId, role, branchId)
Service -> Persistence: Begin transaction; allocate sale number
Persistence -> DB: Read sale sequence and branch settings
DB --> Persistence: Sequence and settings
loop For each requested sale item
  Service -> Persistence: Load eligible branch batches
  Persistence -> DB: Query available batches ordered by expiry
  DB --> Persistence: Batch rows
  Service -> Persistence: Stage batch issue and inventory transaction
end
Service -> Service: Apply discount rules; calculate totals and payment status
alt Insufficient stock or discount reason missing
  Service -> Persistence: Roll back transaction
  Service --> Handler: Throw business exception
  API --> POS: HTTP 400 Bad Request
else All sale checks pass
  Service -> Persistence: Add Sale and SaleItems; SaveChanges
  Persistence -> DB: Insert sale and generate SaleId
  DB --> Persistence: SaleId
  Service -> Persistence: Set SaleId on items; SaveChanges and commit
  Persistence -> DB: Persist items and inventory changes; COMMIT
  DB --> Persistence: Commit complete
  Service -> Audit: Log sale creation
  Service --> Handler: SaleResponse
  Handler --> Mediator: SaleResponse
  Mediator --> API: SaleResponse
  API --> POS: HTTP 200 + SaleResponse
  POS --> Pharmacist: Display completed sale / receipt
end

note over API,POS
  Invalid or missing JWT returns HTTP 401.
  Invalid request items return HTTP 400.
end note
@enduml
